       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's ibuprofen 2400 mg per dose, four times daily, which comes to 9,600 mg/day. That's three times the maximum daily dose for an adult (3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 2,400 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. This amount risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and other toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant a total of 2,400 mg/day. If so, the order would be **600 mg by mouth four times daily**, or 800 mg three times daily.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n1. **600 mg PO QID** (2,400 mg/day)\n2. **800 mg PO TID** (2,400 mg/day)\n3. Another dose and frequency you specify\n4. 2,400 mg PO QID as written, if it's intentional. I'd need you to confirm that explicitly, and I'd add a note documenting the rationale.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
